{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4a4ce750-00da-4a64-ac4e-6c9851e3693b",
    "name": "Zimal Store \u2014 Seller Onboarding (Phase 8b: Store Closure & Reopen)",
    "description": "Phase 8b manual test \u2014 the seller's own way out, and the way back.\n\nBEFORE YOU START\n1) php artisan migrate\n2) keep `php artisan queue:work` running\n3) an APPROVED, ACTIVE store owned by {{seller_email}}\n4) an admin {{admin_email}} who does NOT own that store (C12)\n5) set {{store_name}} to the store's EXACT name \u2014 closing asks for it\n6) set {{store_id}} (run folder 3c, or read it from GET /v1/seller/profile)\n7) OPTIONAL: {{manager_token}} from the Phase 7 collection, for E1 and 2c\n\nTHE POINT OF THIS PHASE\nAn admin could suspend a store, but a seller had no way to leave. Now\nthey do \u2014 and `closed` is a THIRD status, never reusing `suspended`.\nSuspended means the platform stopped them; closed means they walked\naway. Folding both into one value would make the audit trail lie about\nwhich happened, and those two facts are not legally interchangeable.\n\nWHAT CLOSING DOES NOT DO: nothing is deleted. The store record, the\nteam rows and the customer account all survive. Only ACCESS goes.\n\nORDER: 0 (tokens) -> 1 (close) -> 2 (what that changed)\n       -> 3 (ask + admin reopens) -> 4 (the two doors) -> 5 (errors).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
