    {
      "name": "4. C40 \u2014 the two doors must stay apart",
      "description": "A bug that had been sitting in Phase 6 since it was written, and only\nbecame reachable when `closed` was added.\n\nsuspend() asked `status === SUSPENDED` and reactivate() asked\n`status === ACTIVE` \u2014 both correct while ACTIVE and SUSPENDED were the\nonly states. With CLOSED in the enum, a closed store PASSED the\nreactivate check and got flipped to active through the wrong door:\nclosed_at left behind, and the team's roles never restored.\n\nBoth guards now name the state they ALLOW, not the one they reject.\nA `!==` guard silently widens every time a new enum case is added.\n\nTO RUN THIS FOLDER: close the store again first (folder 1c).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4a. Reactivate a CLOSED store -> 409",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/sellers/{{store_id}}/reactivate",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "sellers",
                "{{store_id}}",
                "reactivate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Before C40 this returned 200 and quietly corrupted the store's state.\nReopening a closed store is /reopen, never /reactivate.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{admin_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4b. Suspend a CLOSED store -> 409",
